                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "What I would like to see is a check here. In the simplest a file access /var/lib/fb-ipmi-oem/i2c-readwrite.lock as an example) and only if that file exists should we allow this command to succeed.\n\nIn the longer term, we could maintain a per-bus/addr allow-list as a JSON file.\n\nThat way, we could add this during testing when the functionality is needed and not have it bleed into prod use cases."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/oemcommands.cpp",
                    "line": 2863,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Elton Wang",
                        "email": "elton.wang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "EltonWang-wiwynn"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the comment, we will implement the allow-list mechanism that blocks commands targeting bus/address not on the list in the next patch."
                },
