                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Whats the general use case for this addition ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/oemcommands.hpp",
                    "line": 81,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Elton Wang",
                        "email": "elton.wang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "EltonWang-wiwynn"
                    },
                    "message": "This command was added to support a DFM vendor's requirements for manufacturing testing. The vendor's testing tool runs on the host and requires in-band access to the BMC's I2C bus.\nA similar command already exists in phosphor-host-ipmid, but the standard IPMI specification only allocates 3 bits for the bus number, which is insufficient for most use cases. This new command was introduced to address that limitation.\nRelated discussion on discord: https://discord.com/channels/986224305987784725/986252729410273290/1506909622316040344"
                }
            ],
